    "https://www.uwa.edu/the-university-of-west-alabama-seeks-a-dean-of-the-college-of-liberal-arts/": {
      "title": "The Position",
      "description": "The University of West Alabama seeks a Dean of the College of Liberal Arts | University of West Alabama Skip to content More Schedule a Tour Apply Now Athletics Alumni TigerHub Portal UWA Official Bookstore Schedule a Tour Request Information A-Z Index Students Academics About UWA Admissions & Aid Life at UWA Online Programs Give Back Apply Now The University of West Alabama seeks a Dean of the College of Liberal Arts Home » The University of West Alabama seeks a Dean of the College of Liberal Arts View Position Profile Location Livingston, Alabama The Position The University of West Alabama invites applicants for the position of Dean of the College of Liberal Arts. The Dean is responsible for all matters relating to the instructional programs within the college, including the various courses of study, the teaching faculty, class scheduling, student registration, and physical and financial resources. The Dean works in cooperation with the Department Chairpersons, the other Deans, the Provost, University committees and councils, and other members of the faculty and staff to meet these responsibilities. Responsibilities Coordinates and participates in a continuing, systematic, and broad-based process of planning and evaluation of the educational activities of teaching, advising, research, and public service. Coordinates the preparation of departmental budgets and supervises spending within the college, approving specific expenditures when required by State law or University policy. Coordinates the scheduling of the necessary courses, preparing class schedules each term and submitting them to the Provost, and supervises all instruction offered by the college, both on campus and off. Allots the space and other physical resources assigned to the college for the support of the instructional programs, continuing education activities, and other approved purposes, ensuring compliance with space management policies and procedures. Assigns faculty mentors and supervises the registration of all students in the college. Coordinates curriculum development within the college, aligned with relevant workforce data and the University mission, and ensuring timely student degree completion. Ensures appropriate opportunities for student experiential learning within the college, aligned with program outcomes, workforce needs, and post-graduation student success. Evaluates and approves official student records and requests, including transcripts of transfer students, applications for graduation, exceptional class schedules, and such special requests as those relating to transient student status, correspondence work, etc. Supervises the recruitment of faculty and academic staff, accepting applications, receiving recommendations from Department Chairpersons and search committees, and making recommendations to the Provost. Provides orientation for new faculty and continuing opportunities for faculty development through in-service meetings, consultants, counseling, travel, etc. Participates in the ongoing evaluation of faculty for purposes of development, promotion and tenure decisions, and re-appointment. Maintains records on faculty qualifications, faculty workloads, faculty absences, and related matters and, as required, submits to the appropriate administrative offices the necessary forms and reports relating to faculty, such as faculty evaluation documents, annual sick leave records, payroll forms, travel requests, etc. Coordinates, with the Department Chairperson, the employment of adjunct faculty. Coordinates the annual review of the Planning and Assessment documents for the college. Encourages and coordinates college fundraising and grant writing efforts. Establishes and maintains meaningful relationships with college alumni to support engagement, collaboration, and advancement of the college’s mission. Coordinates student recruitment for the college, working with the Office of Student Recruitment. Submits each year to the Provost a corrected and updated copy of the appropriate sections of the General Catalogue and the Graduate Catalogue. Promotes a culture of active engagement by encouraging and demonstrating regular, visible presence and participation in college-sponsored events, programs, and activities. Provides a means of communication between the faculty and the central administration and oversees internal college communication processes, as well as external communication with institutional leadership. Coordinates the Freshman Studies Program. Coordinates the University Honors Program. Coordinates continuing education and community service programs, workshops, conferences, and related activities within the college. Provides liaison with the public and with the higher education community, serving as a University representative to appropriate professional groups within the State and elsewhere. Performs other duties as requested by the Provost and the President. Qualifications Minimum The terminal degree in a discipline in which the college offers programs. Demonstrated excellence in teaching at the university level. Proven administrative skills. Demonstrated scholarship, research, and/or the equivalent creative professional experiences. Successful experience with grants. Proven communication and interpersonal skills that will enable the candidate to work effectively with students, faculty, other administrators, and external constituencies. Preferred Successful experience in university administration at chairperson level or above. Experience with accrediting agencies on regional and national levels. Experience at a regional university. Experience in online academic offerings. About the College of Liberal Arts The College of Liberal Arts is organized into four departments; the Department of English and History, with majors in English, English Language Arts, History, History with Teacher Certification, Political Science, and General Social Sciences; the Department of Psychology and Sociology, with majors in psychology and sociology; the Department of Communications and Creative Arts, with majors in Integrated Marketing Communications and Creative Arts Enterprise; and the Department of University Studies, which houses the University Honors Program, Freshman Studies, the UWA Basic Curriculum, and academic programs in Interdisciplinary Studies and Professional Studies. The college also houses several minors, including political science and anthropology. The college is home to 516 undergraduate students and 345 graduate students. There are 38 full-time faculty members in the college, 87 percent of whom hold a terminal degree. The Department of Communications and Creative Arts is a dynamic hub where creativity meets communication. Its programs are designed to empower students with the skills and knowledge needed to excel in a rapidly evolving media landscape. Through a combination of theoretical learning and hands-on experience, students explore the art of storytelling, media production, and creative expression across various platforms. The Department of English and History offers profound insights into the human condition and the world we live in. English delves into the art of language, literature, and expression, exploring how written and spoken words shape and reflect culture, thought, and identity. The Department of Psychology and Sociology offers a wide range of learning opportunities. Each field within the department provides unique insight into how and why humans do the things they do. After graduating from UWA, many students move on to graduate school in Psychology, Sociology, Social Work or a closely related field. The Department of University Studies empowers students to explore diverse academic pathways while designing personalized programs aligned with their career goals. Through interdisciplinary studies major, students integrate coursework from multiple fields into a cohesive, purposeful degree. Programs and Initiatives The College of Liberal Arts has several exciting programs and initiatives underway, including: Choir The UWA Choir holds singing auditions each semester for all students to earn up to $3,000 per year in performance scholarships, regardless of their majors, minors, or previous experience. The Choir practices twice a week and regularly performs an eclectic repertoire of choral music, both locally and regionally, from all periods of history and many parts of the world. Vocalists entertain audiences with their musical interpretations in blues, jazz, gospel, madrigals, chants, rock, show tunes, pop, and foreign languages. Theatre The UWA Theatre holds auditions each semester for all students to earn up to $1,800 per year in scholarships, regardless of their majors, minors, or previous experience. There are opportunities for actors, set designers, production assistants, stage managers, videographers, and editors. UWA Writing Center The University of West Alabama Writing Center offers writing assistance to students from any discipline across campus. The Center strives to be a space that nurtures collaborative endeavors and values critical thinking, where writers feel welcomed as intellectuals, recognized as individuals, and appreciated as part of the UWA community. The Sucarnochee Review Established in 1974 and named for the Sucarnochee River that runs near the University of West Alabama, The Sucarnochee Review is published annually by the University’s Department of English and History. It is student-led and student-edited with strong belief in the value of amplifying student voices. It proudly makes space in each issue for new and upcoming undergraduate writers while also being open to writers of all ages, at all stages of their careers. Livingston Press The Press’s goal is to publish contemporary literary novels and story collections. Fort Tombecbe UWA owns the Fort Tombecbe site and more than 23 acres surrounding it. It’s an active archeological dig that gives students in archeology, anthropology, even biology, hands-on experience in the field. Explore the College of Liberal Arts’ programs and initiatives , or learn more about the College of Liberal Arts . Accreditation The University of West Alabama is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges to award associate’s, bachelor’s, master’s, education specialist and doctoral degrees. About The University of West Alabama The University of West Alabama (UWA) was chartered in 1835 as a church-related female academy and remained primarily a school for girls until the twentieth century. 2025 marked 190 years of proud tradition and educational excellence with more than 41,000 graduates. The University of West Alabama is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC) to award associate, bachelor, master, education specialist, and doctoral degrees through the College of Business, Julia Tutwiler College of Education, College of Liberal Arts, College of Natural Sciences and Mathematics, Division of Engineering Technology, Ira D. Pruitt College of Nursing and Health Professions, School of Graduate Studies, and Online Programs. View an interactive campus map. Mission Enriching lives through education, service, and outreach. Vision To offer quality education and effective services while establishing a model for leadership in the region and beyond. Strategic Plan The University of West Alabama’s Strategic Plan 2026–2035, Your Bridge to What’s Possible , outlines a bold vision for advancing student success, access, and institutional growth in rural and regional higher education. The plan prioritizes enrollment expansion, retention, and a personalized student experience supported by flexible learning models, strong partnerships, and data-informed decision-making. Grounded in values of integrity, excellence, collaboration, and regional responsibility, UWA is committed to serving as a catalyst for opportunity and prosperity in the communities it serves. Read more about the strategic plan here. Points of Interest A total of 30 new academic programs have been added over the past 6 years, including 2 doctoral programs (Ed.D. & D.B.A.) Over 100 international students on campus from 41 different countries UWA has been consistently recognized as one of the safest, most diverse, and best value of any public university in the state UWA was awarded the Governor’s Seal of Excellence in Work-Based Learning for its Integrated Marketing Communications Program The Division of Economic & Workforce Development received the American Association of State Colleges and Universities (AASCU) Excellence and Innovation Award for Regional and Economic Development In 2025, UWA was designated as an Opportunity College and University (OCU), reflecting its long-standing commitment to both access and economic outcomes for graduates In 2023, the Alabama Black Belt National Heritage Area was designated; UWA’s Center for the Study of the Black Belt serves as the management entity for this area The institution has received multiple national rankings for best online college, especially at the master’s level in education (e.g., 3rd in the nation for “Best Online Master’s Degrees in Secondary Education”) To Apply Acceptance of inquiries, nominations, and applications will begin immediately and continue until the completion of the search. To apply, please submit a CV and a cover letter that addresses your reasons for interest and related qualifications/experience. Applications will be reviewed as they are submitted. Interested parties are encouraged to apply no later than October 16, 2026 . Apply Online All applications and nominations will be held in confidence. For more information or to make a recommendation or nomination Caitlin Hummel 585-880-7550 [email protected] Before hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation, including information obtained from social media and other internet sources. The University of West Alabama does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, hearing status, personal appearance, color, sex, pregnancy, political affiliation, creed, ethnicity, national origin (including ancestry), citizenship status, physical or mental disability (including perceived disability), age, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, veteran or military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, domestic violence victim status, or any other protected category under applicable local, state, or federal law, including protections for those opposing discrimination or participating in any grievance process on campus, with the Equal Employment Opportunity Commission, or other human rights agencies. AA/EOE. Minority applications encouraged. 100 N. Washington St.,\nLivingston,\nAL 35470 (205) 652-3400 Administration Americans with Disabilities Act A-Z Index Consumer Information Directory Employment Map & Directions Media Reset Your Password Self Service Parking and Traffic Regulations University News Weather © Copyright 2025 University of West Alabama. All rights reserved. Privacy Policy Public & Legal Notices Title IX Sitemap Schedule a Tour Athletics Alumni TigerHub Portal UWA Official Bookstore A-Z Index Search Students Back to Main Menu Prospective Students Accepted Students Go West Orientation Current Students Transfer Students International Students Online Students Family & Guardians Graduation and Commencement Back to Students Apply for Your Degree Event Details Regalia Diploma Information Annual Commencement Honors Map and Directions Watch Live Graduation & Commencement FAQs Academics Back to Main Menu Academics Overview Back to Academics Academics Overview Programs Online Programs Study Abroad Programs Academic Support College of Business College of Education College of Liberal Arts College of Natural Sciences and Mathematics College of Nursing and Health Professions Division of Engineering Technology School of Graduate Studies University Honors Program Academic Resources Back to Academics Julia Tutwiler Library Academic Catalogs Academic Calendars Final Exam Schedule Transcript Request Student Rights and Records About UWA Back to Main Menu Mission & Vision History & Tradition Accreditations Fast Facts Office of the President Board of Trustees Employment Opportunities Caring Campus Initiative Virtual Campus Tour Faculty & Staff Directory University Departments Back to About UWA University Departments Registrar Educator Preparation & Certification Office Student Advocacy Julia Tutwiler Library Institutional Effectiveness & Strategic Planning Information Technology Student Affairs University Police Department Human Resources UWA Printing Services Lifelong Learning and Economic & Workforce Development Institutional Advancement & Alumni Affairs Sponsored Programs, Research & Outreach Communications & Marketing Admissions & Aid Back to Main Menu Admissions Back to Admissions & Aid Admissions First-Time Freshmen Admission Requirements and Application Process Undergraduate Transfer Students Admission Requirements and Application Process Online Students Graduate Students International Students Dual Enrollment Students Financial Aid Back to Admissions & Aid Financial Aid Applying for Financial Aid Scholarships Loan Programs Grants Federal Work Study Veterans’ Assistance Cost of Attendance Enrollment Status & Withdrawal Implications FAFSA Verification Professional Judgment (PJ) Satisfactory Academic Progress Policy Financial Aid FAQ Tuition & Fees Student Accounts Back to Admissions & Aid Student Accounts Pay Your Bill Tuition Payment Plans Financial Aid Disbursements and Refunds Life at UWA Back to Main Menu Campus Life Back to Life at UWA Campus Life Student Involvement Student Life Performing Arts Athletics Greek Life Student Government Association Residence Life Back to Life At UWA Residence Life Incoming Freshman Students Incoming Transfer Students Current Students Housing MyHousing Portal Dining Services Health Information Virtual Campus Tour Online Programs Give Back Students There is an abundance of information that students need to have a successful college experience, in and out of the classroom. Find that information here. Prospective Students Accepted Students Orientation Current Students Transfer Students International Students Online Students Family & Guardians Graduation/Commencement Apply for Your Degree Event Details Regalia Diploma Information Annual Commencement Honors Watch Live Map & Directions FAQs Academics What inspires you? Learn all about UWA’s Colleges and Divisions, our wide range of degree programs, academic support services and even opportunities to study abroad. Academics Overview Programs Online Programs Study Abroad Programs University Honors Program Academic Support College of Business College of Education College of Liberal Arts College of Natural Sciences and Mathematics College of Nursing and Health Professions Division of Engineering Technology School of Graduate Studies Academic Resources Julia Tutwiler Library Academic Catalogs Academic Calendars Final Exam Schedule Transcript Request Student Rights & Records About UWA UWA offers a variety of support services, from help with academic needs and technology issues to ensuring the safety of students, faculty and anyone else on campus. Learn more about our departments. Mission & Vision History & Tradition Accreditations Fast Facts Office of the President Board of Trustees Employment Opportunities Caring Campus Initiative Virtual Campus Tour Faculty and Staff Directory University Departments Registrar Educator Preparation & Certification Office Student Advocacy Julia Tutwiler Library Institutional Effectiveness and Strategic Planning Information Technology University Police Department Human Resources Printing Services Lifelong Learning and Economic & Workforce Development Institutional Advancement Sponsored Programs and Research Communications & Marketing Stud"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193516": {
      "title": "Director of Career Development",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Director of Career Development University of West Alabama: Enrollment Management and Student Success Location University of West Alabama Open Date Sep 14, 2026 Description The Director of Career Development provides leadership for the university’s career development programs and services, supporting students’ career readiness, experiential learning, and post-graduate success. The Director collaborates with academic and student support units to connect academic experiences with workforce preparation and employment opportunities. This position is responsible for developing and implementing programs that enhance career exploration, employability skill development, personal branding, employer engagement, and workforce readiness for students and alumni. The Director uses data-informed practices to support student success outcomes and strengthen relationships with employers, community partners, and alumni. Strategic Planning & Program Development Develop and implement strategic goals for career development services aligned with institutional priorities and workforce needs. Support student career readiness through programs focused on career exploration, employability skills development, personal branding, and career preparation and placement. Use data and assessment practices to evaluate program effectiveness and improve student outcomes related to career readiness and employment. Develop and coordinate experiential learning opportunities, including internships, job shadowing, and employer-sponsored projects. Career Services Operations Manage the daily operations of the Career Development office. Supervise career development staff and support ongoing professional development initiatives. Develop annual goals, assessment measures, and program evaluations for career development initiatives. Manage departmental budget and resources effectively. Oversee career services technologies and resources that support student engagement and employer outreach. Employer & Community Engagement Cultivate and maintain partnerships with employers, alumni, and community organizations to expand experiential learning and career opportunities for students. Coordinate employer engagement activities, including career fairs, networking events, on-campus recruiting, and workshops. Participate in workforce development initiatives and maintain relationships with external partners to support experiential learning and student employment opportunities. Collaboration & Campus Integration Collaborate with academic affairs, enrollment management, student success, and student affairs to support career readiness initiatives throughout the student experience. Partner with academic departments to support the incorporation of career competencies and experiential learning into academic programs. Collaborate with institutional research and other campus partners to track and report career-related outcomes. Support faculty and staff in promoting career development resources and opportunities for students. Qualifications Required Bachelor’s degree in higher education, business, public administration, counseling, or a related field. Minimum of five (5) years of progressive professional experience in career services, workforce development, student success, or related areas in higher education. Demonstrated experience in program development, employer engagement, and staff supervision. Strong understanding of career readiness competencies, employment trends, and workforce development practices. Excellent communication, organizational, and collaboration skills. Preferred Master’s degree in higher education, business, public administration, counseling, or a related field. Experience implementing new programs or initiatives. Experience developing employer partnerships and experiential learning opportunities. Familiarity with career services technologies and assessment practices. Knowledge of regional workforce and economic development trends. Application Instructions To Apply:  When you select Apply Now, you will be prompted to provide the following: Cover letter. A current Resume or C.V. Transcripts of all college work.  Unofficial transcripts will suffice for application.  Official transcripts must be submitted immediately upon employment. Email and phone number of three professional references; reference letters may be requested later. Before hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation, including information obtained from social media and other internet sources. Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement The University of West Alabama does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, hearing status, personal appearance, color, sex, pregnancy, political affiliation, creed, ethnicity, national origin (including ancestry), citizenship status, physical or mental disability (including perceived disability), age, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, veteran or military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, domestic violence victim status, or any other protected category under applicable local, state, or federal law, including protections for those opposing discrimination or participating in any grievance process on campus, with the Equal Employment Opportunity Commission, or other human rights agencies. AA/EO Employer. Minority applications encouraged. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Cookie Details List‎ Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Cookie Details List‎ Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. Cookie Details List‎ Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Cookie Details List‎ Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Confirm my choices"
    },
    "https://www.uwa.edu/the-university-of-west-alabama-seeks-a-dean-of-the-college-of-business/": {
      "title": "The Position",
      "description": "The University of West Alabama seeks a Dean of the College of Business | University of West Alabama Skip to content More Schedule a Tour Apply Now Athletics Alumni TigerHub Portal UWA Official Bookstore Schedule a Tour Request Information A-Z Index Students Academics About UWA Admissions & Aid Life at UWA Online Programs Give Back Apply Now The University of West Alabama seeks a Dean of the College of Business Home » The University of West Alabama seeks a Dean of the College of Business View Position Profile Location Livingston, Alabama The Position The Dean of the College of Business is responsible for all matters relating to the instructional programs within the College, including the various courses of study, the teaching faculty, class scheduling, student registration, and physical and financial resources. The Dean works in cooperation with the Department Chairpersons, the other Deans, the Provost, University committees and councils, and other members of the faculty and staff to meet these responsibilities. Responsibilities Coordinates and participates in a continuing, systematic, and broad-based process of planning and evaluation of the educational activities of teaching, advising, research, and service. Coordinates the preparation of departmental budgets and supervises spending within the College, approving specific expenditures when required by State law or University policy. Coordinates the scheduling of the necessary courses, preparing class schedules each term and submitting them to the Provost, and supervises all instruction offered by the College, both on campus and off. Allots the space and other physical resources assigned to the College for the support of the instructional programs, continuing education activities, and other approved purposes, ensuring compliance with space management policies and procedures. Assigns faculty mentors and supervises the registration of all students in the College. Coordinates curriculum development within the College, aligned with relevant workforce data and the University mission, and ensuring timely student degree completion. Ensures appropriate opportunities for student experiential learning within the College, aligned with program outcomes, workforce needs, and post-graduation student success. Evaluates and approves official student records and requests, including transcripts of transfer students, applications for graduation, exceptional class schedules, and such special requests as those relating to transient student status, correspondence work, etc. Supervises the recruitment of faculty and academic staff, accepting applications, receiving recommendations from Department Chairpersons and search committees, and making recommendations to the Provost. Provides orientation for new faculty and continuing opportunities for faculty development through in-service meetings, consultants, counseling, travel, etc. Participates in the ongoing evaluation of faculty for purposes of development, promotion and tenure decisions, and re-appointment. Maintains records on faculty qualifications, faculty workloads, faculty absences, and related matters and, as required, submits to the appropriate administrative offices the necessary forms and reports relating to faculty, such as faculty evaluation documents, annual sick leave records, payroll forms, travel requests, etc. Coordinates, with the Department Chairperson, the employment of adjunct faculty. Coordinates the annual review of the Planning and Assessment documents for the College. Encourages and coordinates College fundraising and grant writing efforts. Establishes and maintains meaningful relationships with college alumni to support engagement, collaboration, and advancement of the College’s mission. Coordinates student recruitment for the College, working with the Office of Student Recruitment. Promotes a culture of active engagement by encouraging and demonstrating regular, visible presence and participation in college-sponsored events, programs, and activities. Submits each year to the Provost a corrected and updated copy of the appropriate sections of the General Catalogue and the Graduate Catalogue. Provides a means of communication between the faculty and the central administration and oversees internal college communication processes, as well as external communication with institutional leadership. Coordinates continuing education and community service programs, workshops, conferences, and related activities within the College. Provides liaison with the public and with the higher education community, serving as a University representative to appropriate professional groups within the State and elsewhere. Ensures the involvement of the business and industry advisory council with the College’s academic programs. Performs other duties as requested by the Provost and the President. Qualifications Minimum D.B.A. or Ph.D. in a business discipline and/or related terminal degree. Demonstrated excellence in teaching at the university level. Demonstrated scholarship, research, and/or equivalent professional experience. Knowledge of distance-learning technology and ability to lead substantial growth of MBA, DBA, and online programs. Proven communication and interpersonal skills that will enable the candidate to work effectively with students, faculty, other administrators, and external constituencies. Preferred Successful experience in university administration at chairperson level or above. Experience with accrediting agencies on a regional and national level. Experience at a regional university. Successful and innovative approaches to building and sustaining new academic programs, both on-campus and online. Demonstrated experience in engaging business and industry with the College and its academic programs. Experience in local and regional economic development, fundraising, and/or work with advisory boards. About the College of Business The College of Business offers Bachelor of Business Administration degrees in Accounting, Business Administration, Finance, Management, and Marketing. The College also offers the Master of Business Administration and the Doctor of Business Administration. The College has 595 undergraduate students and 310 graduate students. The College has 11 full-time faculty members, 82 percent of whom hold a terminal degree. The College is organized into two departments: Accounting, Finance, and Economics, and Business Administration, Management, and Marketing. The College houses a Small Business Development Center and the Center for Business and Entrepreneurial Services. The Department of Accounting, Finance, and Economics provides a quality education in preparation for jobs in accounting and financial-related careers. The Department has a successful history of placing qualified students in internships and other experiential learning opportunities while working toward degree completion. The Department of Business Administration, Management & Marketing offers majors in business administration (with a choice of emphasis), management and marketing (with a choice of emphasis). The business administration, management and marketing majors are available either online or on campus. Programs and Initiatives The College of Business has several exciting programs and initiatives underway, including: Small Business Development Center The mission of the University of West Alabama’s Small Business Development Center is to grow the economy in the western region of Alabama, known as the Black Belt, by providing entrepreneurs with the education, information and tools necessary to build successful businesses. The Center’s services are targeted to Choctaw, Clarke, Marengo, Sumter, and Wilcox counties. Accounting Club The Accounting Club’s mission is to promote interest in the accounting profession as a career, educate students about the various career paths available to accountants, and to provide opportunities for members to interact with other accounting students, faculty, and leaders in the business community. Enactus Enactus is a network of leaders committed to using business as a catalyst for positive social and environmental impact. Their goal is to educate, inspire and support young people to use innovation and entrepreneurship to solve the world’s biggest problems. At UWA, Enactus students take what they are learning in the classroom and apply those principles in the community to help small businesses and community members thrive. Finance Club The Finance Club provides a forum for students to discuss current events in finance, which will prepare them for interviews and the workplace. Minority Business Student Association The mission of the Minority Business Student Association is to empower and advance minority business majors through networking and collaborating with professionals to better prepare students for their future endeavors. Explore the College of Business programs and initiatives or learn more about the College of Business . Accreditation The University of West Alabama is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges to award associate’s, bachelor’s, master’s, education specialist and doctoral degrees. The College of Business is nationally accredited by the Accreditation Council for Business Schools and Programs (ACBSP) to offer the following degrees: Bachelor of Business Administration (BBA) in Accounting, Business Administration, Finance, Management, and Marketing, and the Master of Business Administration (MBA) degree. About The University of West Alabama The University of West Alabama (UWA) was chartered in 1835 as a church-related female academy and remained primarily a school for girls until the twentieth century. 2025 marked 190 years of proud tradition and educational excellence with more than 41,000 graduates. The University of West Alabama is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC) to award associate, bachelor, master, education specialist, and doctoral degrees through the College of Business, Julia Tutwiler College of Education, College of Liberal Arts, College of Natural Sciences and Mathematics, Division of Engineering Technology, Ira D. Pruitt College of Nursing and Health Professions, School of Graduate Studies, and Online Programs. View an interactive campus map. Mission Enriching lives through education, service, and outreach. Vision To offer quality education and effective services while establishing a model for leadership in the region and beyond. Strategic Plan The University of West Alabama’s Strategic Plan 2026–2035, Your Bridge to What’s Possible , outlines a bold vision for advancing student success, access, and institutional growth in rural and regional higher education. The plan prioritizes enrollment expansion, retention, and a personalized student experience supported by flexible learning models, strong partnerships, and data-informed decision-making. Grounded in values of integrity, excellence, collaboration, and regional responsibility, UWA is committed to serving as a catalyst for opportunity and prosperity in the communities it serves. Read more about the strategic plan. Points of Interest A total of 30 new academic programs have been added over the past 6 years, including 2 doctoral programs (Ed.D. & D.B.A.) Over 100 international students on campus from 41 different countries UWA has been consistently recognized as one of the safest, most diverse, and best value of any public university in the state UWA was awarded the Governor’s Seal of Excellence in Work-Based Learning for its Integrated Marketing Communications Program The Division of Economic & Workforce Development received the American Association of State Colleges and Universities (AASCU) Excellence and Innovation Award for Regional and Economic Development In 2025, UWA was designated as an Opportunity College and University (OCU), reflecting its long-standing commitment to both access and economic outcomes for graduates In 2023, the Alabama Black Belt National Heritage Area was designated; UWA’s Center for the Study of the Black Belt serves as the management entity for this area The institution has received multiple national rankings for best online college, especially at the master’s level in education (e.g., 3rd in the nation for “Best Online Master’s Degrees in Secondary Education”) To Apply Acceptance of inquiries, nominations, and applications will begin immediately and continue until the completion of the search. To apply, please submit a CV and a cover letter that addresses your reasons for interest and related qualifications/experience. Applications will be reviewed as they are submitted. Interested parties are encouraged to apply no later than October 16, 2026. All applications and nominations will be held in confidence. Apply Online For more information or to make a recommendation or nomination: Angelyn P. Gay 541-880-4914 [email protected] Before hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation, including information obtained from social media and other internet sources. The University of West Alabama does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, hearing status, personal appearance, color, sex, pregnancy, political affiliation, creed, ethnicity, national origin (including ancestry), citizenship status, physical or mental disability (including perceived disability), age, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, veteran or military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, domestic violence victim status, or any other protected category under applicable local, state, or federal law, including protections for those opposing discrimination or participating in any grievance process on campus, with the Equal Employment Opportunity Commission, or other human rights agencies. AA/EOE. Minority applications encouraged. 100 N. Washington St.,\nLivingston,\nAL 35470 (205) 652-3400 Administration Americans with Disabilities Act A-Z Index Consumer Information Directory Employment Map & Directions Media Reset Your Password Self Service Parking and Traffic Regulations University News Weather © Copyright 2025 University of West Alabama. All rights reserved. Privacy Policy Public & Legal Notices Title IX Sitemap Schedule a Tour Athletics Alumni TigerHub Portal UWA Official Bookstore A-Z Index Search Students Back to Main Menu Prospective Students Accepted Students Go West Orientation Current Students Transfer Students International Students Online Students Family & Guardians Graduation and Commencement Back to Students Apply for Your Degree Event Details Regalia Diploma Information Annual Commencement Honors Map and Directions Watch Live Graduation & Commencement FAQs Academics Back to Main Menu Academics Overview Back to Academics Academics Overview Programs Online Programs Study Abroad Programs Academic Support College of Business College of Education College of Liberal Arts College of Natural Sciences and Mathematics College of Nursing and Health Professions Division of Engineering Technology School of Graduate Studies University Honors Program Academic Resources Back to Academics Julia Tutwiler Library Academic Catalogs Academic Calendars Final Exam Schedule Transcript Request Student Rights and Records About UWA Back to Main Menu Mission & Vision History & Tradition Accreditations Fast Facts Office of the President Board of Trustees Employment Opportunities Caring Campus Initiative Virtual Campus Tour Faculty & Staff Directory University Departments Back to About UWA University Departments Registrar Educator Preparation & Certification Office Student Advocacy Julia Tutwiler Library Institutional Effectiveness & Strategic Planning Information Technology Student Affairs University Police Department Human Resources UWA Printing Services Lifelong Learning and Economic & Workforce Development Institutional Advancement & Alumni Affairs Sponsored Programs, Research & Outreach Communications & Marketing Admissions & Aid Back to Main Menu Admissions Back to Admissions & Aid Admissions First-Time Freshmen Admission Requirements and Application Process Undergraduate Transfer Students Admission Requirements and Application Process Online Students Graduate Students International Students Dual Enrollment Students Financial Aid Back to Admissions & Aid Financial Aid Applying for Financial Aid Scholarships Loan Programs Grants Federal Work Study Veterans’ Assistance Cost of Attendance Enrollment Status & Withdrawal Implications FAFSA Verification Professional Judgment (PJ) Satisfactory Academic Progress Policy Financial Aid FAQ Tuition & Fees Student Accounts Back to Admissions & Aid Student Accounts Pay Your Bill Tuition Payment Plans Financial Aid Disbursements and Refunds Life at UWA Back to Main Menu Campus Life Back to Life at UWA Campus Life Student Involvement Student Life Performing Arts Athletics Greek Life Student Government Association Residence Life Back to Life At UWA Residence Life Incoming Freshman Students Incoming Transfer Students Current Students Housing MyHousing Portal Dining Services Health Information Virtual Campus Tour Online Programs Give Back Students There is an abundance of information that students need to have a successful college experience, in and out of the classroom. Find that information here. Prospective Students Accepted Students Orientation Current Students Transfer Students International Students Online Students Family & Guardians Graduation/Commencement Apply for Your Degree Event Details Regalia Diploma Information Annual Commencement Honors Watch Live Map & Directions FAQs Academics What inspires you? Learn all about UWA’s Colleges and Divisions, our wide range of degree programs, academic support services and even opportunities to study abroad. Academics Overview Programs Online Programs Study Abroad Programs University Honors Program Academic Support College of Business College of Education College of Liberal Arts College of Natural Sciences and Mathematics College of Nursing and Health Professions Division of Engineering Technology School of Graduate Studies Academic Resources Julia Tutwiler Library Academic Catalogs Academic Calendars Final Exam Schedule Transcript Request Student Rights & Records About UWA UWA offers a variety of support services, from help with academic needs and technology issues to ensuring the safety of students, faculty and anyone else on campus. Learn more about our departments. Mission & Vision History & Tradition Accreditations Fast Facts Office of the President Board of Trustees Employment Opportunities Caring Campus Initiative Virtual Campus Tour Faculty and Staff Directory University Departments Registrar Educator Preparation & Certification Office Student Advocacy Julia Tutwiler Library Institutional Effectiveness and Strategic Planning Information Technology University Police Department Human Resources Printing Services Lifelong Learning and Economic & Workforce Development Institutional Advancement Sponsored Programs and Research Communications & Marketing Student Affairs Admissions & Aid All the information you need before giving us your application, including access to several financial aid resources, fees, supporting documentation needs and links to our Application Portal. Admissions First-Time Freshmen Undergraduate Transfer Students Online Students Graduate Students International Students Dual Enrollment Students Financial Aid Apply for Financial Aid Scholarships Loans Grants Federal Work Study Veterans' Assistance Cost of Attendance Enrollment Status & Withdrawal Implications FASFA Verification Professional Judgement Satisfactory Academic Progress Financial Aid FAQ Tuition & Expenses Student Accounts Pay Your Bill Tuition Payment Plans Refund Information Life at UWA Your UWA education is so much more than going to class. Learn more about the countless opportunities to be"
