    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189046": {
      "title": "Director of Marketing",
      "description": "Department: University of West Alabama: Communications and Marketing Location: University of West Alabama The Director of Marketing provides leadership for the University's marketing function, overseeing the development and execution of strategies that support enrollment, advancement, engagement, and institutional priorities. This role is responsible for connecting University goals with the needs of key audiences through coordinated marketing initiatives, audience-focused campaigns, digital engagement, and creative services. Working collaboratively with the Director of Communications, the Director of Marketing ensures that marketing efforts align with institutional messaging, brand standards, and strategic objectives while providing leadership for marketing personnel, web operations, creative services, and external marketing partnerships. Duties and Responsibilities Develop and implement integrated marketing strategies that support institutional priorities, including enrollment growth, advancement initiatives, alumni engagement, student engagement, community engagement, and University visibility. Provide leadership and direction for the University's marketing operations, including advancement marketing, web content management, digital engagement initiatives, and creative services. Collaborate with the Director of Communications to ensure alignment between institutional messaging, content strategy, brand standards, and audience engagement efforts. Lead the planning and execution of marketing campaigns that support recruitment, fundraising, events, academic initiatives, and other strategic University priorities. Oversee the University's primary marketing efforts for Enrollment Management, Institutional Advancement, and other campus partners, ensuring marketing strategies are aligned with organizational goals and audience needs. Provide strategic leadership and institutional coordination for enrollment marketing initiatives, including managing external strategic partners, agencies, and consultants, and supporting all undergraduate and graduate student recruitment efforts. Establish priorities, expectations, and performance measures for external marketing partners and evaluate effectiveness in support of enrollment goals and institutional objectives. Oversee the University's primary web presence and assigned digital platforms through supervision of the Web Content Specialist or other staff as appropriate, ensuring digital properties support institutional objectives, audience needs, brand compliance, accessibility standards, and user experience expectations. Provide leadership for the University's visual identity, creative services, and development of marketing and engagement materials that support institutional priorities. Ensure effective stewardship of institutional marketing resources, including creative assets, digital platforms, vendor relationships, and marketing technologies assigned to the division. Utilize available data, audience insights, and performance measures to evaluate marketing effectiveness and identify opportunities for continuous improvement. Establish and maintain systems, workflows, and service standards that improve project management, prioritization, collaboration, and responsiveness across marketing functions. Supervise and develop assigned personnel, fostering a culture of collaboration, innovation, accountability, and service excellence. Required Bachelor's degree in Marketing, Communications, Business, Public Relations, or a related field. Minimum of five (5) years of progressively responsible professional experience in marketing, communications, enrollment marketing, advancement marketing, public relations, or a closely-related field. Minimum of two (2) years of experience leading projects, teams, programs, vendor relationships, or organizational initiatives. Demonstrated experience developing and implementing marketing strategies, campaigns, or audience engagement initiatives. Experience collaborating with multiple stakeholders and managing competing priorities in a complex organizational environment. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Preferred Master's degree in Marketing, Communications, Business Administration, Higher Education Administration, or a related field. Seven (7) or more years of progressively responsible professional experience in marketing, communications, enrollment marketing, advancement marketing, or closely related areas. Three (3) or more years of supervisory or leadership experience with responsibility for personnel, budgets, vendor relationships, or strategic initiatives. Experience working in a higher education marketing environment. Experience in higher education marketing, enrollment management, institutional advancement, or nonprofit marketing. Experience managing creative services, web content, digital platforms, or integrated marketing campaigns. Experience working with external marketing agencies, consultants, or vendor partners. Experience utilizing marketing analytics, audience insights, or performance metrics to inform decision-making and strategy. FLSA : Exempt Before hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation, including information obtained from social media and other internet sources. To Apply: When you select \"Apply Now,\" you will be prompted to provide the following: Cover Letter. A current resume or CV. Transcripts of all college work. Unofficial transcripts will suffice for application.  Official transcripts must be submitted immediately upon employment. Email and phone number of three professional references.  Reference letters may be requested later."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192617": {
      "title": "Director of TRIO Student Support Services (Grant Funded)",
      "description": "Department: University of West Alabama: Enrollment Management and Student Success Location: University of West Alabama The Director of TRIO Student Support Services provides overall leadership and management of the program; the development, implementation, and evaluation of policies, procedures, and all program activities; staff hiring, training, evaluation, and supervision; and the maintenance of collaborative relationships with the faculty, staff, and University administrators. Overseeing all budget operations and fiscal reports; assuring that all milestones are completed and all objectives are met, that planning and evaluation reports are completed, and that new grants are written. The director will oversee the grant to ensure compliance and exemplary service delivery. Responsibilities : Knowledge of grant guidelines and regulations; ability to interpret and explain regulations, policies, procedures, guidelines, and reporting requirements particular to TRIO/D.O.E. funded programs. Strong positive interpersonal skills; able to work collaboratively, build effective working relationships, be a team-oriented leader, and problem solver. Sensitivity and understanding of diverse populations relevant to educational, socioeconomic, cultural, and ethnic backgrounds. Knowledge and understanding of challenges that psycho/socio behaviors face by 1st generation, income-eligible, and/or disabled students in pursuit of higher education. Effective coaching, managing, mentoring, and motivating skills that support the grant, accomplish the college mission, and support staff with individual professional goals. Plan, implement, coordinate, and evaluate program services and activities to ensure grant objectives are continually being met. Manage the identification, selection, assessment, and notification process for student participants. Plan and coordinate promotion of the program to campus audiences. Plan and conduct retention-directed activities and events. Develop, implement, evaluate, and resource specialized curricula promoting student academic success with formative and summative assessments. Coordinate and oversee documentation services, program compliance, performance, research, and data collection of student outcomes related to grant objectives. Establish working relationships with college departments, divisions, and administration. Program liaison to TRIO conferences, trainings, Department of Education Program Officer, campus committees, and meetings. Perform any other duties as required in fulfillment of the grant requirements. This is a grant-funded position.  No guarantee or commitment is made regarding future or continued employment beyond the grant award or the terms of the contract. Required Master’s degree from an accredited institution in education, guidance and counseling, or a related field. Three to five years of experience administering postsecondary programs, including experience with budget management and program assessment. Preferred Experience working with TRIO/SSS-eligible students. Demonstrated professional achievement or recognition for outstanding accomplishments. Experience providing counseling, academic coaching, advising, or related student support services. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Demonstrated academic achievement. Familiarity with the University of West Alabama and its service area. Knowledge of college core curriculum, student retention theories, and research-based practices that support student success. Understanding of or personal experience with challenges similar to those faced by TRIO participants. Experience with grant writing and proposal development. Experience with educational research, assessment, program evaluation, or data analysis. Demonstrated organizational and leadership skills. Experience developing and delivering presentations, workshops, or training. To Apply:  When you select Apply Now, you will be prompted to provide the following: Cover letter. A current Resume or C.V. Transcripts of all college work.  Unofficial transcripts will suffice for application.  Official transcripts must be submitted immediately upon employment. Email and phone number of three professional references; reference letters may be requested later. Before hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation, including information obtained from social media and other internet sources."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192618": {
      "title": "Director of Second-Year Experience",
      "description": "Department: University of West Alabama: Enrollment Management and Student Success Location: University of West Alabama The Director of Second-Year Experience provides strategic leadership for the university's comprehensive second-year student success initiatives designed to improve persistence, academic progression, career readiness, and graduation outcomes. The Director leads the planning, implementation, assessment, and continuous improvement of programs that support sophomore students as they confirm academic and career pathways, engage in high-impact learning experiences, and successfully transition toward upper-division coursework. The Director collaborates across Academic Affairs, Student Affairs, Enrollment Management, Career Development, faculty, advisors, and external partners to develop an integrated second-year experience that advances institutional retention and student success goals. The Director serves as the university's primary leader for second-year student success strategy, using data-informed decision-making to strengthen student engagement, persistence, and workforce readiness. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Strategic Leadership and Program Administration Provide strategic leadership for the university's Second-Year Experience program and related student success initiatives. Develop and implement a comprehensive second-year success strategy aligned with institutional priorities. Establish annual goals, performance metrics, and assessment plans to improve second-to-third-year retention and student success outcomes. Develop policies, procedures, and operational practices that enhance the sophomore student experience. Identify opportunities for innovation and continuous improvement through assessment and evidence-based practices. Student Success, Retention, and Academic Progression Lead university initiatives that promote academic progression, major confirmation, career planning, and student engagement. Develop targeted retention strategies for second-year students using predictive data and student success indicators. Partner with academic advisors, faculty, and student support offices to coordinate intervention strategies for students experiencing academic or personal barriers. Monitor persistence trends and recommend institutional strategies to improve student success and retention. Career and Academic Pathway Leadership Lead initiatives that assist students in confirming academic majors and career goals. Collaborate with Career Development, academic departments, and employer partners to strengthen academic and career pathway development. Expand participation in internships, undergraduate research, job shadowing, experiential learning, and employer-connected learning opportunities. Provide leadership for the implementation and continuous enhancement of CAPE career pathway initiatives. Campus Collaboration and Partnership Development Foster strong partnerships across Academic Affairs, Student Affairs, Enrollment Management, Career Development, and external organizations to create a seamless second-year student experience. Serve on university committees related to student success, retention, advising, and career readiness. Build relationships with employers, alumni, and community partners that enhance experiential learning and workforce preparation. Represent the university in regional and national initiatives focused on student success and sophomore retention. Assessment, Data Analysis, and Continuous Improvement Develop and oversee a comprehensive assessment framework for second-year student success initiatives. Analyze institutional data related to retention, persistence, engagement, career readiness, and student outcomes. Prepare executive reports and recommendations for university leadership that demonstrate program effectiveness and progress toward institutional and grant objectives. Utilize assessment findings to guide strategic planning, resource allocation, and program enhancement. Supervision and Resource Management Supervise graduate assistants, student employees, and peer mentors, as applicable. Provide leadership in staff development, performance management, and program coordination. Assist in developing and managing departmental budgets. Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by University leadership. Required Master's degree Five years of progressively responsible professional experience in student success, retention, advising, career development, student affairs, or related higher education leadership. Demonstrated experience leading institutional initiatives that improve student persistence, engagement, or academic success. Experience using assessment data to inform strategic planning and decision-making. Excellent leadership, communication, collaboration, organizational, project management, and analytical skills. Preferred Experience supervising staff and managing complex student success initiatives. Experience with employer engagement, experiential learning, and career development programming. Experience utilizing student success technologies and predictive analytics platforms. Knowledge of evidence-based retention strategies, student development theory, and sophomore student success initiatives. To Apply:  When you select Apply Now, you will be prompted to provide the following: Cover letter. A current Resume or C.V. Transcripts of all college work.  Unofficial transcripts will suffice for application.  Official transcripts must be submitted immediately upon employment. Email and phone number of three professional references; reference letters may be requested later. Before hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation, including information obtained from social media and other internet sources."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189571": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach: Tennis",
      "description": "Department: University of West Alabama: Athletics Location: University of West Alabama The University of West Alabama (UWA) is seeking a dedicated and knowledgeable Assistant Tennis Coach to join our athletics staff. This position will assist the Head Coach in all aspects of the tennis program, including recruitment, training, teaching, game preparation, and administrative duties. The ideal candidate will have a passion for developing student-athletes both on and off the court while upholding the values of the University and the athletic department. On the court coaching responsibilities assigned by the Head Coach. Recruiting duties assigned by the Head Coach Other administrative and coaching duties assigned by the Head Coach and Athletic Director. Essential: Bachelor’s Degree. Successful coaching experience. Ability to recruit student-athletes to a Division II tennis program. Proven ability to develop tennis players. Knowledge of NCAA regulations- Division II and Gulf South Conference preferred. Ability to work effectively with administration, faculty, coaching staff, students, alumni, and boosters. Desired: Master’s Degree. Knowledge of NCAA Division II and Gulf South Conference regulations and recruiting guidelines. To Apply :  When you select Apply Now, you will be prompted to provide the following: Cover Letter. A current résumé. Transcripts of all college work.  Unofficial transcripts will suffice for application.  Official transcripts must be submitted immediately upon employment. Email and phone number of three professional references; reference letters may be requested later. Before hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation, including information obtained from social media and other internet sources."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189648": {
      "title": "Assistant Men's Soccer Coach",
      "description": "Department: University of West Alabama: Athletics Location: University of West Alabama The University of West Alabama is accepting applications for the Assistant Men's Soccer Coach position.  This is a full-time position.  The selected candidate will be responsible for assisting the Head Men's Soccer Coach with the operation of all facets of a successful Division II Men's Soccer program.  Duties include, but are not limited to: Organizing practice and match plans for the men's soccer program. Coordinate scheduling and recruiting activities. Assist with financial aid and eligibility matters for student-athletes. Other duties assigned by the Head Coach and Athletic Director. Required: Bachelor’s Degree. Collegiate soccer experience as a player and/or a coach. Excellent communication and organizational skills. Ability and desire to motivate student-athletes to succeed academically. Ability to work effectively with administration, faculty, coaching staff, students, and alumni. Desired: College coaching and recruiting experience. Knowledge of NCAA rules and regulations. Master’s Degree or other advanced education. Prior to hiring, the final candidates must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation, including information obtained from social media and other internet sources. To Apply :  When you select Apply Now, you will be prompted to provide the following: Cover Letter. A current resume. Transcripts of all college work.  Unofficial transcripts will suffice for application.  Official transcripts must be submitted immediately upon employment. Email and phone number of three professional references; reference letters may be requested later."
